#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
===============================================================================
KHARE 2022 CASE I n-DODECANE SHOCK-DROPLET ANALYSIS
===============================================================================

Purpose
-------
Analyze AMReX/yt plot files for the Redding and Khare 2022 Case I style setup:
    n-dodecane droplet, Ms = 6.5 shock, vaporization enabled.

This script is written specifically from the uploaded input file
"UResKhare2022_CaseI" and the requested result directory:

    /mmfs1/home/spatel6/flames/bin/tests/FlowPatel/
    256Ultra_Res_CFL_0.1_Khare2022_CaseI_nDodecane_Ms6p5_Vap

Notes from the input file
-------------------------
    Domain:                 x,y in [0.020, 0.060] m
    Droplet center:          (0.040, 0.040) m
    Initial droplet radius:  R0 = 4.4e-3 m
    Initial droplet diameter D0 = 8.8e-3 m
    Eta convention:          eta approximately 0 inside liquid,
                             eta approximately 1 in surrounding vapor/gas
    Liquid density:          rho_l = 749.5 kg/m3
    Gas/vapor density:       rho_vapor = 1.35598311723 kg/m3 pre-shock,
                             rho_shock = 39.0 kg/m3 post-shock
    Surface tension:         sigma = 0.025 N/m
    Vaporization:            apply_vaporization = 1

Outputs
-------
1. Time-series plots:
    - Projected liquid area vs time
    - Aspect ratio vs time
    - Surface area proxy vs time
    - Liquid and vapor mass fractions vs time
    - Liquid remaining and vapor mass change vs time
    - diagnostics.csv

2. Field visualizations:
    - Numerical schlieren of pressure
    - Numerical schlieren of temperature
    - Numerical schlieren of velocity magnitude
    - Optional GIFs for each schlieren sequence

Important interpretation
------------------------
This is a 2D calculation. The quantity labeled "surface area" here is the
2D diffuse-interface measure

    A_2D = integral |grad eta| dA

which has units of length in a 2D simulation. It is best interpreted as
interface length, or surface area per unit out-of-plane depth. It is not a
true 3D droplet surface area unless an additional geometric assumption is made.

===============================================================================
"""

